Good morning,

Would it be possible to see the source material for the ectotherm flight model?

I'd like to test whether I can use (or how to change) the flight model for a beetle (the dung beetle Onthophagus taurus). They fly infrequently as the minimum flight temperature is relatively high, and they will otherwise crawl to forage.

I'm also hoping for some clarity on how flight speed is incorporated into the model. Once, the beetle has found a cow pat, it will remain for approx. 24 hours. Food density, assimilation, ingestion and handling time should remain consistent regardless of behaviour, although the time to locate food and the energetic cost of different modes of locomotion differs.

I understand the model is untested and have done some behavioural and energetic assays I can use to ground truth.

Thanks in advance!

Cheers,
Alex

