> A quick update on that second point that Mike brought up: this has now been just addressed, mcera5 now automatically handles either new or old variable names of ERA5 (these variables don't exist in ERA5-land). If you are using an old query of ERA5, please re-install mcera5 and then micro_era5() should work:
>
> devtools::install_github("dklinges9/mcera5")
>
> As users of mcera5 and micro_era5() may have noted, the ECMWF Climate Data Store (CDS) has been undergoing a lot of changes in the past 6 months, and this may continue as they keep ironing out kinks. Please do notify me (by submitting an issue on the mcera5 GitHub <https://github.com/dklinges9/mcera5>) if you face issues pertinent to mcera5, but first make sure you are using the most updated version of mcera5.
>
> Best,
> Dave
