> On Fri, Mar 28, 2025 at 8:27 AM NicheMapR <nich...@googlegroups.com> wrote:
> > Dear NicheMapR users,
> >
> > I recently pushed a change to NicheMapR on github to allow hourly rather than daily shade vectors to be passed to the ectotherm model. If you are using the latest github version and have code that specifies the shade manually, it may need updating to account for this.
> >
> > Re the variable name changes in ERA5 that were discussed in an earlier thread, if you do have old downloads (pre Jan 2025) of ERA5, micro_era5 won't work with them because the mcera5 package has been updated to only recognise the new variable names. One workaround is to simply change the variable names in the old era5 files manually with NCO <https://nco.sourceforge.net/>. Here's an example loop in R to do this:
> >
> > files<-list.files()
> > files<-files[grep(".nc", x = files)]
> > for(i in 1:length(files)){
> >   filenm <- files[i]
> > cmd<-paste0("ncrename -h -O -v msdwlwrf,avg_sdlwrf ", filenm)
> > system(cmd)
> > cmd<-paste0("ncrename -h -O -v msnlwrf,avg_snlwrf ", filenm)
> > system(cmd)
> > }
> >
> > All the best,
